{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1467647-sascha-myca-vykos-was-in-the-order-of-hermes-holy-fucking-shit","id":1467647,"title":"Sascha/Myca Vykos was in the Order of Hermes!?!?!?!?! Holy fucking shit!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-11-12T23:13:27-08:00","id":1467647,"title":"Sascha/Myca Vykos was in the Order of Hermes!?!?!?!?! Holy fucking shit!","content":"I seriously just found this out! <br /> <br /> Can any one give me reference to a book this is in. <br /> <br /> I just read Constantinople by Night and it doesn't even mention it there<br /> <br /> if you have any doubts, wiki the character and see for yourself. <br /> <br /> id seriously like to find out more about his backstory. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-13T00:02:11-08:00","id":1467653,"title":"","content":"Never heard of it before, but Vikos is cited in many places.<br /> <br /> Anyways, it seems he was just a sorcerer, not an Awakened, and it isn't all that spectacular. Getting into Goratrix's bad side isn't especially hard, either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-13T00:45:09-08:00","id":1467656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1467647-sascha-myca-vykos-was-in-the-order-of-hermes-holy-fucking-shit?p=1467653#post1467653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Never heard of it before, but Vikos is cited in many places.<br /> <br /> Anyways, it seems he was just a sorcerer, not an Awakened, and it isn't all that spectacular. Getting into Goratrix's bad side isn't especially hard, either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rotfl!!! About the goratrix line!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-13T12:06:50-08:00","id":1467702,"title":"","content":"House Tremere's interest in Vykos dates back to when Vykos, Goratrix, and Tremere were all mortals, and when House Tremere was still a part of the Order of Hermes. <br /> <br /> Even in the Dark Ages setting, this is far enough back in history to just merit a brief mention in Vykos' biographies from a few books here and there. I think it mostly serves as a bit of trivia to take the Tzimisce/Tremere feud and make it very, very personal for one of the game's signature characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-15T06:41:55-08:00","id":1467876,"title":"","content":"In the Tzimisce clanbook revised, it's mentioned that some wizards of House Tremere were Embraced in the Tzimisce clan, before the start of the war between the two factions. In a version of history of Sasha Vykos, it'said that Myca Vykos was a wizard of House Tremere, and her noble background was important for House Tremere to be introduced in Transylvania. Myca was betrayed by his rival Goratrix, who handed him over to the vampires of the Tzimisce clan, but Symeon Obertus decided to Embrace him rather than murder him. Symeon planned to use Myca to replace the absent Dracon as Michael of Constantinople's lover.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2250-magus","name":"Magus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-13T03:15:42-07:00","id":1505240,"title":"","content":"So a friend of mind started spouting \u201cso Vykos would know all about the order of Hermes even in the modern era then?!\u201d<br /> <br /> to which I was like, \u201cno not really, just because he was a member doesn\u2019t mean that the tzimisce would know much at all about the order and even Vykos himself might be badly misinformed about hermetic magi as well in my opinion.<br /> <br /> and also, would Vykos even be able to remember that much about the Order.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","user":"Zennis","date":". 03-13-2023, 06:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-13T10:08:58-07:00","id":1505258,"title":"","content":"I've heard it mentioned enough times that he was a magi of some sort and that he and Gotrix didn't get along and it was bad enough that the later conspired to have Vykos get in trouble with the fiends. But it backfired because he got embraced by Symeon a grandchilde of Dracon and they didn't act like your &quot;typical&quot; Tzismce and he spent his early nights in Constantinopile instead of fiend central. It's quite likely that he doesn't know how the order works now and would be working with knowledge a 1,000+ years out of date.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-19T22:59:37-07:00","id":1505884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1467647-sascha-myca-vykos-was-in-the-order-of-hermes-holy-fucking-shit?p=1505258#post1505258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've heard it mentioned enough times that he was a magi of some sort and that he and Gotrix didn't get along and it was bad enough that the later conspired to have Vykos get in trouble with the fiends. But it backfired because he got embraced by Symeon a grandchilde of Dracon and they didn't act like your &quot;typical&quot; Tzismce and he spent his early nights in Constantinopile instead of fiend central. It's quite likely that he doesn't know how the order works now and would be working with knowledge a 1,000+ years out of date.</div> </div> </div> </div>My point exactly","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}